From 209b5c5ea12c2d1f328214335d10e466b9dbb2d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qingh097 <qingh097@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 15:41:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add videogen observation pipeline: offline BC and online
 image-model DAgger

Train the vision student on generated RGB instead of ray-traced rendering.

- distill_trainer_videogen.py: TRLDistillTrainerVideoGen with collect / offline /
  online / image_dagger modes. image_dagger relabels all three camera views every
  rollout step via a warm Image3F server, rendering envs in parallel and mixing in
  ray-traced envs at videogen.raytraced_mix_prob.
- image3f_frame_client.py / videogen_client.py: length-prefixed pickle clients for
  the render servers. The frame client re-reads its endpoint file on every reconnect
  so a restarted server heals a run in progress.
- isaacsim.py: conditioning cameras for the renderer (per-view depth, robot RGB and
  semantic masks), and optional scene walls giving the head camera real background
  geometry. Walls default to non-collidable: collidable walls sit in the robot's
  walking path and cost ~40 points of success rate (16.7% collidable, 56.0% none,
  60.0% visible but non-collidable). Set cameras.wall_collisions to restore the old
  behaviour.
- configs for collection, offline BC and image DAgger.

Measured on walk_stand_place_grasp_turn_homie, ray-traced observations under the
offline-BC eval config: offline BC 57.3% (150 eps), image DAgger 69.3% (300 eps).
Generated observations are policy-equivalent to ray tracing -- a policy that never
trained on them scores 59.3% vs 57.3%.

Note eval_agent_trl.py loads config.yaml from the checkpoint's own directory, so a
DAgger checkpoint must be staged beside the baseline config or it is scored in a
different environment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
