 ```
 
+### Student Training Without Ray Tracing (generated observations)
+
+Ray-traced RGB is too slow to keep inside the DAgger loop at scale. Two alternatives are
+implemented here, both documented with launch commands, configs and pitfalls in
+[`../README.md`](../README.md) (`fast_roborender/`):
+
+- **Offline BC** (`+exp=loco_manip/wsdpt_videogen_offline_bc`) — behaviour-clone on a
+  pre-rendered dataset of generated frames.
+- **Online image-model DAgger** (`+exp=loco_manip/wsdpt_image_dagger`) — a warm Image3F
+  server relabels all three camera views every step
+  (`gr00t/rl/trl/trainer/distill_trainer_videogen.py`, `videogen.mode: image_dagger`).
+
+Generated observations are policy-equivalent to ray tracing on this task (59.3% vs 57.3%
+for a policy that never trained on them), and online DAgger reaches 69.3% vs 57.3% for the
+offline-BC baseline (300 vs 150 episodes).
+
+> **Two traps worth knowing before you run either.**
+> `eval_agent_trl.py` loads `config.yaml` from the *checkpoint's own directory*, so
+> evaluating a DAgger checkpoint against its own run config silently compares two
+> different environments — always stage the checkpoint beside the baseline's config.
+> And `cameras.add_scene_walls` must be paired with `cameras.wall_collisions: false`
+> (the default): collidable backdrop walls block the robot's path and cost ~40 points
+> of success rate.
+
 ## Configuration
 
 This project uses [Hydra](https://hydra.cc/) for configuration. Configs are composed from YAML files in `gr00t/rl/config/`. Override any value from the command line:
